--- PATCH NOTES ---
-- File: scripts/webm.lua (applies to encode() function, L1790-1796)
-- Also applies to: re-workspace/canonical/webm.lf.lua (same lines)
--
-- Problem (FIND-011):
--   The existing code blindly appends every whitespace-separated token from
--   additional_flags and non_strict_additional_flags to the encode command array.
--   If a token lacks a leading '--' it is treated by mpv as a positional argument
--   (a filename to play), not as an option flag. The user's config contained:
--     additional_flags= cq-level=28
--   which produced the bare token "cq-level=28" — mpv tried to open a file named
--   "cq-level=28", failed, and the encoder exited with code 1.
--
-- Fix:
--   Before appending each token, check whether it begins with '--'. If it does not,
--   emit a warning via mp.msg.warn() and skip the token. The warning is visible in
--   the mpv console (and in the log file if log-file= is configured) so the user
--   can identify and correct their configuration.
--
-- Design choice — SKIP vs PREPEND:
--   An alternative would be to prepend '--' automatically: "--" .. token.
--   This is NOT done here because:
--     1. The token may be a bare value (e.g., a filename accidentally entered),
--        not a flag name. Prepending '--' would create a nonsense flag.
--     2. It silently modifies user intent. A warning and skip forces the user to
--        supply the correct flag syntax explicitly.
--     3. Some tokens may be codec suboptions (e.g., "crf=28" without "--ovcopts-add=")
--        which cannot be corrected by simply prepending "--".
--
-- The same validation is applied to non_strict_additional_flags for consistency.
--
-- Impact: Zero impact on correctly-formatted configs (all tokens start with '--').
--         Protects against silent encode failures from misconfigured flags.
